Subject: [LOCAL] media: ov08x40: retry the initial reset once after timeout

The Yoga OV08X40 rapid-reopen failure was captured before any frames with
CCI IRQ_STATUS=0, CUR_CMD=0x01030139, CUR_WORD_CNT=1, EXEC_WORD_CNT=3 and
REPORT_STATUS=0. The command is the initial write 01 03 01 (software reset).
The CCI timeout path resets the stalled controller before returning.

Repeat only that idempotent initial reset, once, and only for ETIMEDOUT.
Do not retry NACK, other errors, mode tables, controls or stream-on writes.
Preserve the second error and all existing startup cleanup.

This is a local workaround for this observed CCI behaviour, not an
upstream-approved generic sensor retry policy. On 2026-11-17 the combined
recovery set passed 10 rapid RGB opens (15 frames each) and 10 IR opens
(30 frames each), with exact counts and no WARN/Oops or stream failures.
Nine initial RGB reset timeouts were recovered. The physical timeout remains
possible and adds about 100 ms to a recovered open; it is not eliminated.
Promoted to updates/ after that test. Normal current boot then passed with
90 RGB metadata frames and separate 1800-buffer RGB and IR PipeWire captures
to EOS. One initial RGB reset timeout was recovered, with no kernel WARN/Oops
or stream failures and no WirePlumber restarts.

--- a/drivers/media/i2c/ov08x40.c
+++ b/drivers/media/i2c/ov08x40.c
@@ -1920,6 +1920,10 @@
 	/* Get out of from software reset */
 	ret = ov08x40_write_reg(ov08x, OV08X40_REG_SOFTWARE_RST,
 				OV08X40_REG_VALUE_08BIT, OV08X40_SOFTWARE_RST);
+	/* The CCI timeout path resets a stalled controller. Reset is idempotent. */
+	if (ret == -ETIMEDOUT)
+		ret = ov08x40_write_reg(ov08x, OV08X40_REG_SOFTWARE_RST,
+					OV08X40_REG_VALUE_08BIT, OV08X40_SOFTWARE_RST);
 	if (ret) {
 		dev_err(ov08x->dev, "%s failed to set powerup registers\n",
 			__func__);
